.TH FBVIEW 1 "July 25, 2026"
.SH NAME
fbview \- display a JPEG image on a ReBSD DRM framebuffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fbview
.I image.jpg
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fbview
streams a baseline JPEG image, scales it to fit the current
.IR /dev/fb0
mode while preserving aspect ratio, clears the framebuffer, and draws the image
using the pixel format reported by the driver.  XRGB8888 and RGBA5551
framebuffers are supported.
.PP
Large images are decoded in MCU blocks directly into the framebuffer.
The decoder selects 1/2, 1/4, or 1/8 JPEG downscaling when appropriate, so
memory consumption does not grow with the full decoded image size.
.PP
Progressive and lossless JPEG files are not supported.
.PP
The current framebuffer mode can be selected with
.BR fbset (1).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /dev/fb0
DRM framebuffer device.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fbset (1)
